# HARD — Full chat visibility (no dropdowns, no collapsed output)

**Scope:** Email processing chat (`EMAIL-PROCESSING-AGENT.md`). Overrides all convenience parallel-tool habits.

## Global rule — everything visible, always (operator demand)

**Every piece of agent output — extracts, processing steps, 7-step RE, status messages, all communication with the operator — must appear as plain visible text in the main chat thread.**

### Banned forever (any case, any turn)

- **Dropdown menus** / collapsed "Finished N background tasks" panels hiding any case content
- **Task / explore subagent output** used as the delivery vehicle for RE, extract, or operator messages
- **Tool-result-only output** — if the operator can only see content by expanding a tool dropdown, it failed
- **"background tasks" panels** containing extract or 7-step text the operator must click to open
- **Any agent turn** where all substantive content is inside collapsed UI and the visible chat shows only a one-liner or nothing

**If it requires a click to expand → it does not exist for the operator. Rewrite as visible chat prose immediately.**

### Past cases

All prior Fall # extracts and 7-steps hidden in dropdowns are **lost from the operator's view** and cannot be recovered by scrolling collapsed panels. That is the failure mode this rule permanently prevents. Every Fall # from now on gets its own fully visible block in the main chat — no exceptions, no matter how many cases are processed in a session.

---

## Mandatory visible paste (EMAIL) — EVERY CASE, EVERY TIME

**Applies to every Fall # forever:** case 1 after login, case 2+, case 100+, after Anwenden, after Weiter/Extern/Next, after `--await-arm`, after typed **RE**, after sidetray click — **EVERY EMAIL case**.

There is **no** "sometimes", **no** "only when recovery", **no** "operator already knows", **no** "file on disk is enough".

After **each** EMAIL extract for **each** new Fall #:

The compound response after extract MUST contain, as **plain visible markdown text before LF tools**:

1. **`CHANNEL: EMAIL`** + **this** Fall #
2. **Full 7-step RE** — sections **1–7**
3. One-line note at the end: `Auto-LF filing now — best-guess: Transfer [Nein/Ja to X]. Reiterate if needed.`

**Do NOT paste the customer email body / Subject / From into chat.** Operator sees it in Sprinklr. The 7-step is the deliverable.

**Auto-LF runs in the background** (`re_complete_sound_hook` → `auto_lf_after_re.py`) after the agent writes sections 1–7. Operator sees the 7-step immediately and can start working in Citrix.

**Every case. Every time. Zero exceptions. Zero delay. Zero waiting for the operator to ask where it is.**

Prior cases' extracts/7-steps do **not** count. A new Fall # = paste extract + 7-step again for **that** Fall #.

### Forbidden post-extract chat (hard ban)

Do **NOT** send only lines like:

- `CHANNEL: EMAIL — Fall #…. extracted. Full 7-step next.`
- `Extract done — writing RE…`
- `RE_TEXT_ONLY_GATE — next message = 7-step`
- Any ack that **promises** the extract/7-step without **pasting** them

If those words appear without the extract + sections 1–7 in the **same** visible message → **you failed**. Fix immediately: paste extract + full 7-step now.

### Forbidden — Auto-LF / tools before 7-step text (2026-09-13 incident)

**Never** run `fill_case_tracker.py` / `--closeout-*` / LF tools for a new EMAIL Fall # until the **full 7-step is already visible** in the main chat for that Fall #.

Especially banned on shell-completion / “briefly inform… follow-up” notifies:

1. Reading terminal → running Auto-LF **without** writing 7-step text first  
2. `--once` / Grep / attachments **instead of** writing 7-step text  
3. Quoting `LF done` when sections 1–7 were never written for that Fall #

**Order lock:** see `.cursor/rules/re-before-auto-lf.mdc`. If only one message is possible → **paste 7-step**; defer LF. Never LF-without-RE.

### Also forbidden

1. **explore/Task** reading terminal capture files (`Explored ….txt`)
2. **Read** of `.cursor/projects/.../terminals/*.txt` instead of `run.py` Shell stdout
3. **Tools + 7-step in one message** (hides under background tasks)
4. **7-step / extract only inside tool output**
5. Stopping after extract and idling until the operator types again
6. **fill_case_tracker before** 7-step text for that Fall # (see above)

## Auto-start (operator does NOT type RE for case 2+)

The agent starts turns **A→B→C automatically** when:
- **`--await-arm`** returns EMAIL extract, or
- **First case after login** is visible (`FIRST_RE_ONCE_PENDING` → agent runs `--once`), or
- Operator types **RE** (first case / recovery)

Do **not** wait for the operator to type **RE** before extract, extract-paste, 7-step, or Auto-LF (except first-case **RE** after login per operator-minimal-input).

## Immediate post–sidetray-click (EMAIL)

When stdout shows **`CASE_ITEM_AUTO_CLICKED`** + **`SIDETRAY_EMAIL_PROCESSING_IMMEDIATE`**:

1. Script already clicked the new EMAIL sidetray item and is extracting **in the same automation run**.
2. On **`DETACHED_ARM_EXTRACT_READY`** / **`RE_TEXT_ONLY_GATE`**: **immediately** turn B = **paste extract + full 7-step** — **no pause**, no "waiting for RE", no extra operator message.
3. After writing sections 1–7: STOP. Background chain (re_complete_sound_hook → auto_lf_after_re.py) files LF + arms closeout silently.

**Hard ban:** Stopping after sidetray click or extract without pasting extract + 7-step + Auto-LF for that Fall #.

## Compound-response protocol (EMAIL) — text-only agent, background LF

**Model (current):** Agent response is always text-only. Background chain handles LF + arm.

**Why no LF tools in agent response:** Long-running `--closeout-anwenden` in the same turn as
the 7-step text causes Cursor to group everything into a “Finished background tasks” dropdown,
permanently hiding the RE from the operator. Text-only avoids this entirely.

### After [AUTO_PIPELINE] — ONE agent response (text-only)

| Phase | What | Renders as |
|-------|------|------------|
| **1** | Read `latest_extract.md` (fast tool) | Tool result (collapsed OK — not operator-facing content) |
| **2** | Write `CHANNEL: EMAIL / Fall #` + **sections 1–7** as plain markdown. End: `Auto-LF filing now.` **STOP.** | 7-step **always visible** |

**Background chain (no agent involvement):**
`re_complete_sound_hook` detects section 7 → spawns `auto_lf_after_re.py` → `fill_case_tracker.py` + `--closeout-*` + Dexter.
Path B (hook) silently spawns `auto_lf_after_re.py` if sound hook missed it — no chat message.

**Micro-template (agent response):**

```
CHANNEL: EMAIL
Fall #…

**1. Case summary**
…
**7. Summary of response**
…
Auto-LF filing now.
```

**Hard bans:**
- Task/explore subagents
- `fill_case_tracker` / `--closeout-*` tools in the same agent response as the 7-step
- `[AUTO_PIPELINE_TURN_C]` — obsolete, blocked, must not be processed
- Tools-only response with no visible 7-step for a new EMAIL Fall #

## Operator recovery

| Operator types | Agent / system |
|----------------|----------------|
| **`RE SHOW`** / **`visible RE`** | Re-print **extract + full 7-step** as **plain main-chat text** |
| **`RE FILE`** | Run `uv run python .cursor/skills/sprinklr-read-answer-email/show_latest_re.py` |
| **Open file** | `.cursor/state/latest_re_visible.md` or `latest_extract.md` (backup only — never a substitute for pasting) |

**Auto picker** often spawns explore → switch to **Composer 2.5** or **Sonnet** (named) if trays persist.

## Agent self-recovery

If tools/Auto-LF already ran with **no** visible extract + 7-step for this Fall # in the main thread:

1. **STOP** further close-out
2. Output **extract + full 7-step now** as plain chat text
3. Continue play-ready / Auto-LF / PR / arms (skip duplicate LF if already done)

